module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.a_per_function_claim_run_refuses_a_modeled_frame_for_a_missing_dispatcher_name

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { BelowCeiling, FoundBelowTheLadder, RecurringFailureMode, RungRead }
import gunbc.guarantee_rung { MechanicallyPreventable }
import gunbc.rung_climb { ClimbableButUnbuilt }

data a_per_function_claim_run_refuses_a_modeled_frame_for_a_missing_dispatcher_name: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "a_per_function_claim_run_refuses_a_modeled_frame_for_a_missing_dispatcher_name" as NonEmptyStr,

  rung: RungRead { found_at: FoundBelowTheLadder, standing: BelowCeiling { current: FoundBelowTheLadder, ceiling: MechanicallyPreventable, blocker: ClimbableButUnbuilt, trigger_capability: "every run that can install a modeled operation realization already carries the dispatcher's own by-name dependencies in its loaded index -- modeled_realization_admitted_in, operation_realization_duplicate and operation_realization_index (v1_interpreter.rs 10644/10669/10729) plus the dispatch-time operation_handler_selection and virtual_clock_after -- so a per-function claim run (gunbc run --claim-run --function) of a modeled-frame witness installs its frame instead of refusing it. Sufficient for: a control that exercises a modeled frame gives the same verdict under the per-function runner and under claim_batch." } },
  receipts: [
    "INVALID STATE: a modeled-realization witness claim run IN ISOLATION (gunbc run --claim-run --function <f>) never installs its frame. The interpreter's modeled-realization dispatcher resolves its OWN dependencies BY NAME -- via run_in_context_with_args -- against ctx.indexes.fn_nodes, which build_scope_indexes_with_module_order fills from the PER-ROOT requested scope. For an isolated claim those dispatcher-internal names are absent from fn_nodes, so evaluate_in_witness_frame refuses; a witness that maps WitnessRefused to a benign Ended (bracket_run_over -> BracketRunEnded) then reads outcomes_of as the empty list.",
    "HARM: with all_settled over [] vacuously true (fixed in the same PR, see the all_settled empty-means-false guard), every leg-harness claim of the file returned the wrong boolean, IDENTICALLY on main and on the repaired branch -- so the node's red control could not discriminate red from green and the whole witness file's controls failed as a set on both trees. Fail-closed in outcome (a refusal, not a wrong answer) but it silently removes the controls' discriminating power.",
    "THE EXACT CAUSE LINE (observed as the bracket_run_over BracketRunEnded cause for test.claim.runner.runner_host_cap_bracket_witness a_transport_with_no_answer_refuses_the_release under gunbc run --claim-run --function): 'no declaration named modeled_realization_admitted_in in this execution loaded index (searched the modules loaded for this run; the name may be declared in a module this run did not load)'. The by-name lookups are at v1_interpreter.rs run_in_context_with_args for modeled_realization_admitted_in (10644), operation_realization_duplicate (10669) and operation_realization_index (10729), with operation_handler_selection and virtual_clock_after reached during dispatch.",
    "EVIDENCE IT IS NOT THIS NODE'S HARNESS: the CI-green test.claim.modeled_filesystem_witness frame claim two_contenders_for_one_unit_get_one_hold FAILS THE SAME WAY under the same per-function runner (gunbc run --claim-run --function), and that witness references NONE of the dispatcher names -- so witnesses are not expected to hand-load them; they resolve only under claim_batch's broad closure scope. The defect is the per-function claim scope not carrying the dispatcher's hidden string-keyed dependencies, not any authored witness.",
    "OPEN, REPAIR NOT IN THIS NODE: make any run that can install a modeled realization load the dispatcher's by-name dependencies (or route those lookups so they do not depend on the per-root scope). claim_batch already does, via its broad one-closure-per-tree scope, which is why CI is green; the per-function path does not. Filed as its own node by crisp-dove-117. The companion all_settled empty-means-false fix (test.claim.runner.runner_host_cap_bracket_witness a_release_that_settles_nothing_is_never_read_as_all_settled) removes the fail-open that disguised this refusal as success, but is necessary-not-sufficient: under the per-function runner the modeled frame still never installs.",
  ],
  evidence: [],
}
